# q38-27b-exl3-ladder.recipe -- the EXL3 size ladder: Qwen3.8-27B served by qwen35_exl3 (plugin ABI 27),
# one rad-convert per published point of turboderp's conversion, ONE recipe for all nine.
#
#   rad-convert <Qwen3.8-27B bf16 checkpoint> \
#       --recipe recipes/q38-27b-exl3-ladder.recipe \
#       --set quantization_config.quant_method=exl3 \
#       -o q38-27b-exl3-<SIZE>bpw.rad
#
# run with EXL3_SRC pointing at the matching turboderp branch (turboderp/Qwen3.8-27B-exl3,
# branch SC_<SIZE>bpw_<HASH>), RELATIVE to where rad-convert runs, so the container records a
# name and not a machine path:
#
#   EXL3_SRC=turboderp/Qwen3.8-27B-exl3/SC_2.20bpw_...   # per point; see tools/make_exl3_ladder.sh
#
# `bits=` is deliberately ABSENT: the exl3 quantiser is import-only (the trellis is exllamav3's,
# read from $EXL3_SRC), and with no bits= it reads K from each weight's own trellis in the source
# (last dimension 16*K). That is what makes one recipe serve the whole ladder, each point at its own
# K (1.40..6.00 bpw, K 1..8 per tensor). `codebook=mul1` is every published point's marker.
#
# The set Qwen's releases quantise, in this tree's qwen35_exl3 names: the attention q|gate, k, v
# and output; the delta net's qkv, z and out (ssm_qkv: this tree's GDN block serves the a|b
# projections plain bf16 beside it -- the fused in_proj_a|b is not in 128s at this model -- so
# they carry no rule and keep the checkpoint's encoding); the MLP's gate and up, STACKED at
# import into one gate_up (the exl3quant quantiser's ffn_gate_up rule: the gate half in rows
# [0, n_ff) on the suh plane, the up half on suh.1 -- the dense kernel's stacked path) feeding
# silu_mul, and down; and the lm_head.
blk.*.attn_qg.weight                 exl3 src=$EXL3_SRC codebook=mul1
blk.*.attn_k.weight                 exl3 src=$EXL3_SRC codebook=mul1
blk.*.attn_v.weight                 exl3 src=$EXL3_SRC codebook=mul1
blk.*.attn_output.weight            exl3 src=$EXL3_SRC codebook=mul1
blk.*.ffn_gate_up.weight           exl3 src=$EXL3_SRC codebook=mul1
blk.*.ffn_down.weight             exl3 src=$EXL3_SRC codebook=mul1
blk.*.ssm_qkv.weight              exl3 src=$EXL3_SRC codebook=mul1
blk.*.ssm_z.weight               exl3 src=$EXL3_SRC codebook=mul1
blk.*.ssm_out.weight             exl3 src=$EXL3_SRC codebook=mul1
output.weight                       exl3 src=$EXL3_SRC codebook=mul1
